`criticalValue` is the constant phase, `orientation` is the sign of its
nondegenerate quadratic part, and `transportedAmplitude` is the sum of the
two half-chart amplitude pullbacks.  The `transport` field is the actual
change-of-variables identity (normally proved with
`intervalIntegral.integral_deriv_smul_comp`), so this interface does not hide
the key analytic transport step behind an unproved reduction theorem. -/
